<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Sanmina slips.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Sanmina slips.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sanmina Corp fell in after-hours trade Monday after the circuit board maker released third quarter earnings, traders said.</p>
<p>Dealers said Sanmina traded at 68 after the bell, down from an unofficial close of 68-5/8.</p>
<p>Sanmina posted quarterly diluted earnings of $0.54 per share, compared with $0.40 per share for the year ago period.</p>
<p>Elsewhere stocks traded in line with closing prices. &quot;There's nothing really trading out-of-whack as of yet,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
</text>
